**Set it up on your Pixel:**

1. **Install CrookCatcher** from <a href="https://play.google.com/store/apps/details?id=com.harteg.crookcatcher&referrer=utm_source%3Dwebsite%26utm_medium%3Dguide%26utm_campaign%3Dpixel-who-tried-to-unlock" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Google Play</a>. There's no account to create.
2. **Allow Device admin.** CrookCatcher uses this permission only to know when an unlock attempt fails.
3. **Allow camera and location access.**
4. **Connect a Gmail account** for the alert emails. CrookCatcher can only *send* emails from it, not read them.
5. **Test it.** Lock your Pixel, enter a wrong PIN on purpose, then unlock it. Your own photo should appear in the app and your inbox.

You choose how many wrong attempts it takes before CrookCatcher acts. Since 2014, CrookCatcher has been downloaded more than 12 million times, and it takes around 1.2 million intruder photos a day.

## Frequently Asked Questions

### Q: Can a Pixel show failed unlock attempts?
A: No. Your Pixel counts wrong guesses only to time the lockouts, and it never shows them. To keep a record with a photo, time and location, you need an app like CrookCatcher.

### Q: How many wrong PIN attempts does a Pixel allow?
A: On recent Android versions, the first 4 wrong guesses have no wait, then the waits grow from 1 minute to days. After 20 wrong guesses no more are allowed. Android 17 is stricter.

### Q: What if I'm locked out of my own Pixel?
A: Google's only option is to erase it, either remotely with Find Hub or with the buttons in Recovery Mode. Afterwards you can restore from your Google Account backup if you know the PIN or pattern from the time of the backup.

### Q: Does a Pixel have an intruder photo feature?
A: No. Pixel's theft protection locks the phone after failed attempts or a snatch, but it doesn't photograph the person or keep a list of attempts.

### Q: Does CrookCatcher work with Pixel's fingerprint and Face Unlock?
A: Yes, you can keep using them. CrookCatcher reacts to a wrong PIN, pattern or password. Failed fingerprint or face attempts don't trigger it.

### Q: Will the person see that they were photographed?
A: CrookCatcher works in the background without a camera preview. Your Pixel shows a small indicator while the camera is in use; that's a system feature apps can't hide.

